   "evidence": "Roadmap \u00a75.2 (`NuclearMedium/README.md:1079-1081`, \"At order four, `vn{4}` \u2026 the fourth root of the negative of the four-particle cumulant\") and \u00a75.3 (`:1097`) are explicit targets; the Bilandzic et al. \u27e84\u27e9 expansion cited by this PR contains the cross term `Re(Q_{2n} conj(Q_n)\u00b2)`, whose pair expectations are over characters of indices `2n` and `n` at distinct particles \u2014 exactly the case the single-index form excludes. Mathlib's lemma at `upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Probability/Independence/Integration.lean:380-385` imposes no relation between `f` and `g`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Probability/Fourier/AddCircle.lean",
   "fix": "Take two indices: `theorem integral_fourier_mul_conj_fourier (hXY \u2026) (hX \u2026) (hY \u2026) (m n : \u2124) : \u222b \u03c9, fourier m (X \u03c9) * conj (fourier n (Y \u03c9)) \u2202P = (\u222b x, fourier m x \u2202\u03bc) * conj (\u222b x, fourier n x \u2202\u03bd)` \u2014 the existing proof goes through verbatim with `f := fourier m`, `g := conj \u2218 fourier n`. Likewise `integrable_fourier_mul_conj_fourier (hX) (hY) (m n : \u2124)`; its current proof routes through `fourier_eval_sub`, so replace it with `Integrable.of_bound` at bound `1` using `norm_fourier_eval` on each factor.",
   "issue": "`integral_fourier_mul_conj_fourier` uses the same index `n` in both factors while deliberately allowing two different laws `\u03bc \u2260 \u03bd`. The conclusion `(\u222b fourier n \u2202\u03bc) * conj (\u222b fourier n \u2202\u03bd)` factorises completely; the proof (via Mathlib's fully general `IndepFun.integral_fun_comp_mul_comp`, which takes unrelated `f : \ud835\udce7 \u2192 \ud835\udd5c`, `g : \ud835\udce8 \u2192 \ud835\udd5c`) never relates the two indices. Same coupling at `integrable_fourier_mul_conj_fourier` (line 63). In a generic `Mathematics/Probability/Fourier/` file this under-generalisation forces a second, near-identical lemma later.",
   "line": 38
  }
 ],
